From 8ab8935644d6e06049baf5754814ac80bbbc6e10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leon Bollerup <mail@r2x2.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:46:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] serve: opt-in automatic shared-prefix candidates after
 the tools, and as requested evidence

Agent clients send no cache breakpoints. The automatic system-head candidate ends before the tool
declarations, which Gemma 4 renders after the system text, so every new session reads the tools
again; and as DefaultAutomatic evidence it is written only into spare capacity, which a cache full
of agent conversations never has. --auto-tools-shared-prefix adds a candidate after the last tool
(its own marker, so tool-order stabilization still holds); --auto-shared-prefix-requested gives the
system and tools candidates RequestedAutomatic evidence, so the planner may evict inactive owners
for them when its net gain is positive. Both are off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
