diff --git a/docs/reference/serving.md b/docs/reference/serving.md
index c73b0a0..a5d15ed 100644
--- a/docs/reference/serving.md
+++ b/docs/reference/serving.md
@@ -1022,6 +1022,14 @@ the four marker slots: when a request also carries the most explicit breakpoints
 explicit one is dropped, as for the last-content candidate. `prompt_cache_options.mode: "explicit"`
 never adds it. `--no-auto-system-shared-prefix` turns it off for both protocols.
 
+`--auto-tools-shared-prefix` adds one more automatic candidate after the last tool declaration.
+Gemma 4's template renders the tools after the system head, so the system candidate alone leaves
+them to be read again by every new session. It takes a marker slot like the system candidate.
+These automatic candidates are `DefaultAutomatic`: they are written only into spare capacity.
+`--auto-shared-prefix-requested` gives the system and tools candidates `RequestedAutomatic`
+evidence instead, so a full cache may evict inactive owners for them when the planner's net gain
+is positive.
+
